%U A402294 74,76,78,80,81,83,85,87,88,90,92,94,96,97,99,101,103,104,106,108,110,112,113,115,117,119,121,122,124,126,128,130,131
%N A402294 a(n) = number of internal crevices between the circles in an optimal arrangement of circles achieving A402292(n).
%C A402294 Also the number of internal cells in the corresponding penny graph (or coin graph).  See A402292 for further information.
%H A402294 N. J. A. Sloane, <a href="/A402292/a402292_2.jpg">Optimal arrangements of circles achieving A402292(n) for 1 <= n <= 9</a>. The numbers of internal crevices between the circles are 0, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8 respectively.
%F A402294 a(n) = 0 for n <= 2, thereafter a(n) = 1 + floor(2*n-sqrt(12*n-3)).
%F A402294 For n >= 3, a(n) = A402292(n) - n - 1.
%Y A402294 Cf. A402292, A402293.
